# Calendar and automation

- ICS defaults to dry-run; `--write` only after user confirmation.
- Stable UIDs; only deadlines, confirmed meetings, time blocks, important follow-ups.
- Scheduled discovery is a **Cursor Automation** reading `docs/automation/DAILY_JOB_DISCOVERY.md`;
  rules/commands are not timers and no OS scheduler is wired.
- Automation edits must be committed to `main` — the cloud run uses a fresh checkout.
- No Google Calendar writes without explicit OAuth setup and confirmation.
